<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Husayn Sufi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 1372</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Husayn <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sufism">Sufi</a> was a leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qungrat">Qungrat</a> tribe who made himself independent ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khwarazm">Khwarazm</a> around 1361, as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a> fell into civil war. Ruling from Urgench, he founded the Sufi dynasty and seized southern Khwarazm, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khiva">Khiva</a> and Kath. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a> invaded in 1372 to reclaim those lands, and Husayn died during the siege of Urgench.</p></div>
